description:
## Problem

`packages/swf/src/sprite.ts` emits `StartSound` (tag 15, references sound by char ID) for ALL frame sounds inside symbol timelines, regardless of whether the sound has an AS2 linkage identifier. But `packages/swf/src/compile.ts` correctly checks `soundItem.linkageIdentifier` and uses `StartSound2` (tag 89, references sound by class name) when present (compile.ts lines 2640–2662):

```ts
// compile.ts (CORRECT):
if (soundItem?.linkageIdentifier) {
  const startSound2Body = encodeStartSound2(soundItem.linkageIdentifier, soundInfoOpts);
  writer.writeTag(Tag.StartSound2, startSound2Body);
} else {
  const startSoundBody = encodeStartSound(soundId, soundInfoOpts);
  writer.writeTag(Tag.StartSound, startSoundBody);
}
```

`sprite.ts` has only (lines 891–908):
```ts
// sprite.ts (INCOMPLETE):
const soundId = soundIdMap.get(frame.sound.libraryItemId);
if (soundId !== undefined) {
  const startSoundBody = encodeStartSound(soundId, soundInfoOpts);
  spriteTags.push(encodeTag(Tag.StartSound, startSoundBody));
}
```

## Impact

Sound items with `linkageIdentifier` set (used in shared library / runtime-sharing scenarios) are not correctly emitted inside symbol timelines. The SWF emits a by-char-ID reference instead of the by-class-name reference that runtime-shared libraries require. This is a silent encoding difference.

## Fix

In `sprite.ts` around lines 891–908, mirror the compile.ts pattern:

1. Import `encodeStartSound2` from `./sounds.js`
2. Look up the `SoundItem` from `doc.library.items` to check for `linkageIdentifier`
3. Use `encodeStartSound2(soundItem.linkageIdentifier, soundInfoOpts)` when `linkageIdentifier` is present

The `doc` parameter is already available in `encodeDefineSprite`. The `soundItems` need to be looked up from `doc.library.items` (the `soundIdMap` is available, add a parallel `soundItemMap` or search `doc.library.items`).

## Files

- `packages/swf/src/sprite.ts` — lines 878–908 (StartSound emission in frame loop)
- Reference: `packages/swf/src/compile.ts` lines 2627–2662
